  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA, pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% acc, while config_010 (image, resnet50, singleprofile) achieves only 20.8% acc—essentially at chance level for a 5-class task. This raises a critical uncertainty: is the image modality fundamentally uninformative for this task, or is resnet50 simply a poor encoder? Question: config_013 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) isolates the effect of image encoder quality by changing only the encoder from resnet50 to a stronger pretrained ViT-L, keeping model_setting and profile_setting identical to config_010. Why this is the best next experiment: The answer determines whether the entire multimodal branch (configs 016–051) is worth pursuing or whether budget should be redirected to optimizing the RNA pipeline. If ViT-L also yields near-chance performance, we can confidently deprioritize image-dependent experiments and focus on RNA encoder/aggregation choices. If it substantially improves, multimodal fusion becomes a viable and promising direction. This single experiment resolves a high-level design uncertainty that gates many downstream decisions, making it the most budget-efficient choice given only two completed experiments."
}

